# Store text as LF regardless of what the working tree holds.
#
# Development happens on Windows against a Linux dev container, and
# editors on this side keep writing CRLF back into files. Without this,
# a one-line change lands as a whole-file rewrite in the diff, and
# `gofmt -l` flags files nobody meaningfully touched. Normalizing on
# commit fixes both without anyone having to remember: the checkout can
# be whatever the editor wants, the repository stays LF.
#
# Run `git add --renormalize .` after changing this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures and assets that must survive byte-for-byte. text=auto detects
# most of these on its own; naming them is cheaper than finding out it
# guessed wrong about scripts/random-sample.bin, which is literally
# random bytes and exists to be compared exactly.
*.bin binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
